      "title": "JEE Main 2023 (15 Apr Shift 1)"
    }
  ],
  "question": {
    "text": "Let the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;contain the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></math> and be parallel to the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>. Then the distance of the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>19</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> from the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> measured parallel to the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> is equal to _________.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "26",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Let the Plane containing the line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></math>&nbsp;is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Also, this plane is parallel to the line</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Now normal of the plane will be perpendicular to the line, so using perpendicular condition we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>18</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>So, equation of the&nbsp;Plane will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>:</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>27</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/984044bf-426b-495d-b7e4-ee0523f90945.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 243px;\" /></p><p>Now to find&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>,</p><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>19</mn></mrow><mn>12</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></math></p><p>So, the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>19</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>And&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> lies on plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>12</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>19</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>21</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>36</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>120</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>190</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>105</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>210</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Hence, Distance is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>36</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>576</mn></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>676</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>26</mn></math></p><p>Hence this is the required answer.</p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
